{"kind":"request","text":"NF2 dynamic CLI result boundary\n\nMcpService.call(name,args) permits a configured ApplicationReadCatalogue to answer before the fixed-tool map. A fixed-name overload promising ActResult for every instance would lie. The CLI constructs an ordinary service with no catalogue, but calls that same dynamic entry. Its current renderer checks only some fields and can print undefined for malformed opaque output.\n\nThe source proposal adds a finite checked display union at that existing CLI boundary. It validates only the fields the renderer uses, preserves fixed-constructor outputs and the original CallResult object, and sends malformed output through the existing unresolved-result failure path. This deliberately improves malformed opaque-output handling. Fixed install/status methods remain precisely typed; the display union never claims Native authority or a complete ActResult for every dynamic catalogue.\n\nDoes that checked display union satisfy NF2, leaving a new typed fixed-tool API to NF4? If NF2 needs the direct fixed-tool API now, please rule on its catalogue/mode contract. We will add no unsound overload, mode marker, cast, sidecar or second dispatcher. The rest of NF2 source work continues.\n\nPinned question and four exact base-source facts: /private/tmp/artroom-nf2-dynamic-cli-display-boundary-question-v1-d3cb-20261111/SOURCE.READY.json, SHA-256 150cfe0004d82593f6e1b47eb632a68ee2efbc2442bdb5cb0b941ad28720bbfd. No CLI projection or new API has been implemented.","body":{"conditions":"Choose the truthful typed boundary for NF2's existing dynamic CLI install/status renderer, without an unsound overload or duplicate dispatcher.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}